infinite-patch 1
# Envelope per voice smoke (v0.6 2.14): Chorder plays chords into Analog; a per-voice
# Envelope (short attack, a hold, a curved decay to a low sustain) sweeps each note's
# cutoff from its own note-on, so every chord starts bright and closes down.
node 1 Notes Chorder
  id chords
end
node 2 Synths Analog
  id synth
end
node 3 Modulators Envelope
  id env
  f attackMs 5
  f holdMs 40
  f decayMs 300
  f sustainLevel 0.15
  f releaseMs 200
  f decayCurve 0.6
  b voice 1
end
node 4 Utility Audio Out
  id speakers
end
node 5 Source Shape
  id picture
end
node 6 Utility Output
  id out
end
note synth 0 chords
aud speakers 0 synth
cable out 0 picture
mod synth cutoff env 0 0 1 0.5
